# Demo Application Guidelines

## Overview

The demo application showcases and tests AceUI components using Vite, React Router DOM, and a structured page/section organization.

- **Purpose:** Showcase and test AceUI components
- **Build tool:** Vite
- **Routing:** React Router DOM
- **Styling:** Global CSS (not CSS Modules)

## File Structure

```
demo/
├── src/
│   ├── App.tsx              # Main app with routing
│   ├── main.tsx             # Entry point
│   ├── constants.ts         # Component navigation constants
│   ├── design-tokens.css    # Design tokens (shared with components)
│   ├── index.css            # Global styles
│   ├── contexts/            # React contexts
│   │   └── SidebarContext.tsx
│   └── pages/               # Component showcase pages
│       ├── HomePage.tsx
│       └── {component}/     # Component-specific pages
│           ├── {Component}Page.tsx
│           └── sections/     # Demo sections
│               └── {SectionName}Section.tsx
├── vite.config.ts
└── package.json
```

## Routing Patterns

- Use React Router DOM for navigation
- Routes defined in `App.tsx`
- Component pages: `/button`, etc. (kebab-case)
- Home page: `/`
- URL search params for tabs: `?t={section-id}`

## Page Structure

### Component Pages (`{Component}Page.tsx`)

- Located in `src/pages/{component}/`
- Use sidebar navigation for sections
- Use `useSearchParams` for tab navigation
- Import sections from `sections/` folder
- Use `SidebarContext` for sidebar state
- Use `page-layout` class for pages with sidebar

Example structure:
```tsx
import { useSearchParams } from "react-router-dom";
import { useSidebar } from "../../contexts/SidebarContext";
import DefaultSection from "./sections/DefaultSection";

const SECTIONS = [
  { id: "default", label: "Default", component: DefaultSection },
];

export default function ButtonPage() {
  const [searchParams] = useSearchParams();
  const currentTab = searchParams.get("t") || "default";
  const { isOpen, close } = useSidebar();
  // ...
}
```

### Sections (`{SectionName}Section.tsx`)

- Located in `src/pages/{component}/sections/`
- Default export function component
- Use `demo-section` class for styling
- Use `demo-row` class for horizontal layouts
- Showcase specific component features/variants

Example:
```tsx
import { Button } from "@aceuidev/button";

export default function DefaultSection() {
  return (
    <section className="demo-section">
      <h2>Button · Default</h2>
      <div className="demo-row">
        <Button onClick={() => alert("Clicked!")}>Click me</Button>
      </div>
    </section>
  );
}
```

## Component Integration

- Import workspace components: `import { Component } from "@aceuidev/{component}"`
- Use workspace protocol: `"@aceuidev/button": "*"` in `package.json`
- Components must be added to `vite.config.ts` `optimizeDeps.exclude` array
- Example: `optimizeDeps: { exclude: ['@aceuidev/button'] }`

## Constants

- `COMPONENTS` array in `src/constants.ts` defines navigation
- Format: `{ name: string, path: string }`
- Update when adding new component pages

Example:
```tsx
export const COMPONENTS = [
  { name: "Button", path: "/button" },
];
```

## Contexts

- Use React Context API for shared state
- Create contexts in `src/contexts/`
- Export provider and custom hook
- Example: `SidebarContext` for sidebar open/close state

Pattern:
```tsx
import { createContext, useContext, useState, ReactNode } from "react";

interface ContextType {
  // context properties
}

const Context = createContext<ContextType | undefined>(undefined);

export function ContextProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {
  // implementation
}

export function useAppContext() {
  const context = useContext(Context);
  if (context === undefined) {
    throw new Error("useAppContext must be used within ContextProvider");
  }
  return context;
}
```

## Styling

- Use global CSS files (not CSS Modules)
- `design-tokens.css`: Shared design tokens (same as component library)
- `index.css`: Global application styles
- Use CSS classes for styling:
  - `demo-section`: Container for demo sections
  - `demo-row`: Horizontal layout for demo items
  - `page-layout`: Layout for pages with sidebar
  - `sidebar`, `sidebar-overlay`: Sidebar components

## Adding New Component Pages

When adding a new component showcase:

1. Create page folder: `src/pages/{component}/`
2. Create `{Component}Page.tsx` with sidebar navigation
3. Create sections in `sections/` folder
4. Add route in `App.tsx`:
   ```tsx
   <Route path="/{component}" element={<{Component}Page />} />
   ```
5. Add to `COMPONENTS` in `constants.ts`
6. Add to `pagesWithSidebar` array in `App.tsx` if sidebar needed:
   ```tsx
   const pagesWithSidebar = ["/button", "/{component}"];
   ```
7. Update `vite.config.ts` to exclude component from optimization

## Naming Conventions

- **Pages:** PascalCase (`ButtonPage.tsx`)
- **Sections:** PascalCase with "Section" suffix (`DefaultSection.tsx`)
- **Contexts:** PascalCase with "Context" suffix (`SidebarContext.tsx`)
- **Routes:** kebab-case (`/button`, etc.)
- **Section IDs:** kebab-case (`"default"`, `"custom-styles"`)

## Best Practices

- Keep demo sections focused on one feature/variant
- Use descriptive section names
- Group related demos in same section
- Use `demo-section` and `demo-row` classes for layout
- Import components from workspace packages (`@aceuidev/{component}`)
- Follow existing sidebar pattern for component pages
- Follow accessibility guidelines (see `accessibility.mdc`)
